From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:56:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(items): translate shared Bedrock cooldown categories

Translate protocol 2193 PlayerStartItemCooldown into Java group cooldowns.
Use the same lossless resource identifier conversion for item components
and packets so custom items sharing a category cool down together.

Read registry cooldown components and legacy food cooldown ticks, including
entries that are not data-driven items. Supply native defaults for the
three built-in cooldown items whose registry entries omit component data.
Resource pack definitions provide a fallback for custom item categories.

The 1.26.51.1 dedicated server registry and Script API probe confirm the
native category names, durations and zero-duration reset packet. Java 26.3
uses group identifiers in both the cooldown packet and use_cooldown data.
